188:* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
219:* ''The ember's serving gate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A third gate tier, the serving route, takes its bundle from SK, and the floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched; a pin moves only by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step, and no quiet period ages a pin out. The reason: a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier never mistakes a serving hearth for an unlocked one. The ruling flips on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
271:* ''One sorter, inside the gate, before the verdict.'' Every vessel socket opens through the sealed face gate's attach, verdict and open sequence; the gate sorts before the verdict, so posture reads once at admission and never at share time. `GateSessionChannel` opens only after the verdict (`face-gate.ts`, `gate-session-channel.ts`). One gate stands per (Nexus, route).
341:* ''The gate's two root doors'' (specified in code; no composer calls them until the socket cutover): a floor gate's bundle derives through the floor key's door, which answers at a locked vessel, hands back a fresh child and never the floor key (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`); a sovereign gate's bundle derives through the custody seat's door, which answers only while the seat holds its key (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`). The doors carry two types, so no line swaps them by accident; a root refuses the other tier's door by name; each seat's door refuses the other tier's child; and a weld holds the two mints to the two seats (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
369:* A per-Nexus wire key in two tiers (operator ruling): a floor route's bundle derives from the floor key and answers at a locked vessel; a sovereign route's bundle derives from the sealed custody root and stands only while the vessel stands unlocked. One gate per (Nexus, route), so knock, pin, verdict and posture read per Nexus exactly (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). The serving route's third tier rides train E (`E3`).
491:* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
524:* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`, tags `0x01` to `0x13`) still reads "provisional", owned by no row, while both operators' vessels speak it on every dial (`face-dial.ts`, `face-gate.ts`). It freezes before the bake: the tag table, the fragment bound and the verdict length, with a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none. Pairs with the `W10` research pair, since both move the dial's bytes once. W.

